WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.282
CTEs and windows are most useful when combined into a pipeline.

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:08.717
The first CTE aggregates revenue to department-product grain.

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:13.122
The second stage ranks those product totals inside each department.

00:00:13.122 --> 00:00:16.362
The final query filters to the top ranks.

00:00:16.362 --> 00:00:20.542
Each stage has a different job and a clear row meaning.

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:26.872
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:26.872 --> 00:00:35.147
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:35.147 --> 00:00:42.442
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
